RC-1R sampling run 1 — HARNESS DEFECT (retained as evidence, spec §17)
====================================================================
Command: node scripts/release/rc1-live-local.mjs --trials 5 --out rc1r-live-local.json
Exit: 1 after ~148 s, ZERO trials completed and ZERO trials written.

Cause (from rc1r-local.err):
  TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'trim')
    at textFlagsOf (dist/test/support/rc1_oracle.js:204)
    at localFacts (rc1_oracle.js:255) -> judgeLocalTrial -> trial()

Root cause: the rewritten local harness put the session's final assistant message on the
raw record as `finalAssistantText`, while `Rc1LocalRaw.finalText` is the field the oracle
reads. The first trial was therefore judged with `finalText === undefined`.

Classification: INFRASTRUCTURE_ERROR / ORACLE_INPUT_ERROR. No product behaviour was
observed; no product conclusion may be drawn from this run.

Fixes (both applied before re-sampling):
  1. the local harness populates the oracle's raw shape exactly (`finalText`,
     `stdoutTurnTexts`);
  2. BOTH harnesses now wrap the oracle call in try/catch and record a classified
     `INFRASTRUCTURE_ERROR / ORACLE_INPUT_ERROR` trial, so a future raw-shape drift costs one
     classified trial instead of the whole sample.
